From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:10:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 103/111] A drag sends fewer messages from text runs near the
 pointer

A run beside the pointer reports again only when the place it would
select changed; the run under the pointer still always reports, as it
outranks the others.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/selectable_rich.rs b/src/selectable_rich.rs
index 161d076..b1370c7 100644
--- a/src/selectable_rich.rs
+++ b/src/selectable_rich.rs
@@ -781,7 +781,11 @@ where
                         leaf: self.leaf,
                         grapheme: state.grapheme_near(bounds, near.pointer),
                     };
-                    if let Some(message) = select(Action::Drag(spot, in_window(near))) {
+                    // Only a new spot, or the leaf under the pointer, which outranks the rest
+                    if (near.is_over()
+                        || selection.is_some_and(|selection| selection.focus != spot))
+                        && let Some(message) = select(Action::Drag(spot, in_window(near)))
+                    {
                         shell.publish(message);
                     }
                 }
